From ba00b7dfeacc362745b196a076edb292f9650b76 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 17:25:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(disclosure): put the FAQ answers back in the HTML, on 275
 pages
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Found by auditing rendered word counts, not by reading source. /faq measured
142 words of main content while displaying eighteen questions, which made no
sense until I looked at what was actually in the <body>.

@radix-ui/react-accordion unmounts the content of a closed item. Measured on
the built output:

  /faq            53 data-state="closed" nodes, 0 answers in <body>
  /               0 answers in <body>
  /areas/barrie   0 answers in <body>

The answer text existed in exactly two places: the RSC flight payload, which
is inside a <script> and is not page content, and the FAQPage JSON-LD. Google
executes JavaScript but does not click accordions. So on 275 pages — the
homepage, /faq, 8 service pages, 224 service x city pages, 32 city hubs and 9
method pages — the rendered body carried every question and not one answer.

That is every FAQ this shop has written, which is the long-tail phrasing
those pages exist to rank for, discarded by a component choice. The JSON-LD
kept Google's FAQ understanding partly intact, which is why nothing looked
broken; an answer engine reading HTML saw questions with nothing under them.

Rebuilt components/ui/accordion.tsx on native <details>/<summary>, keeping
the exported API so no call site changed. Content is in the DOM open or shut,
the browser supplies correct disclosure semantics, and it is a server
component now — so those pages stop shipping an accordion library.

Given up, both stated in the component: exclusive open (native `name` needs a
shared id a server component cannot mint, and reading two answers at once is
not worse), and the open/close animation — which was already dead, since the
classes named animate-accordion-up/down and no such keyframes exist anywhere
in this repo.

Body words:  /faq 142 -> 721.  / 1,614 -> 2,193.
             /services/hardwood-stairs ~626 -> 989.
             /services/hardwood-stairs/vaughan ~626 -> 804.
             /areas/barrie 981 -> 1,085.

First-load JS went DOWN at the same time, because the dependency left with it:
/, /areas/[city], /services/[slug] and /services/[slug]/[city] all 148 -> 140
kB; /faq 126 -> 117 kB. Shared bundle unchanged at 103 kB.
@radix-ui/react-accordion removed from package.json and the lockfile.

No test caught this because every FAQ assertion was about the DATA — questions
unique, answers non-empty, bands agreeing — and none asked whether the answer
survived rendering. tests/disclosure.test.ts now asserts the mechanism:
native <details>, no accordion library in the imports, the dependency absent
from package.json, and AccordionContent never gating its children on open
state, which is the original bug written as a rule.

313 tests pass (308 before). 393 pages, audit clean. 8 routes x 4 viewports,
no horizontal overflow. Disclosure verified working with JavaScript disabled:
18 details, first answer 368 chars in the DOM, summary click still opens it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DNw2m5xoC4nVhuAs5WuzDG
